{"id":"c56","kind":"derived","text":"운동 기록 앱에서 low 와 max 의 차이는 명세가 없을 때 65.5분(1.5분 대 67분), 명세를 주었을 때 63분(16분 대 79분)으로 비슷하고, 달라진 것은 low 가 1.5분에서 16분으로 늘어난 쪽이다","verdict":"derived","scope":"w1 §Building with effort 의 carousel 단계 표시와 /config 단락","derived_from":["1.5","67","16","79"],"note":"원문에는 이 차이가 없다. 문서가 67-1.5=65.5, 79-16=63 으로 계산했다","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Underspecified build task","quote":"low(1.5 min)medium(4 min)high(11 min)max(67 min)"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Highly specified build task","quote":"low(16 min)medium(22 min)high(33 min)max(79 min)"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Lightly specified design task","quote":"At max effort (which took 28 minutes), I got a mockup that looked very much like Claude Code, along with a bunch of walkthroughs for different flows."}]}
{"id":"c58","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 는 세션의 effort 를 명시적 선택(CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL, --effort, 세션의 /effort), 저장한 설정(모델마다 저장한 단계나 effortLevel 키), 모델의 기본값 순으로 보고 처음 정해진 것을 쓴다","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w2 §Adjust effort level 의 결정 순서","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Adjust effort level","quote":"Claude Code resolves the session's effort level in this order, taking the first that applies:"},{"source":"w2","locator":"§Adjust effort level","quote":"An explicit choice: the [`CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars#variables) environment variable, launching with `--effort`, or `/effort` in the session"},{"source":"w2","locator":"§Adjust effort level","quote":"Your settings: the level you saved for the model or an [`effortLevel`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference#effortlevel) key"}]}
{"id":"c59","kind":"web","text":"조직이나 사용자가 정한 effort 상한은 단계를 제한하고, frontmatter 의 단계도 그 상한 안에서 돈다","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w2 §Adjust effort level, §Set the effort level","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Adjust effort level","quote":"Your organization or your own settings can also cap the levels a model offers"},{"source":"w2","locator":"§Set the effort level","quote":"A [`maxEffortLevel`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference#maxeffortlevel) or [organization effort cap](#organization-effort-limits) still limits the level the skill or subagent runs at."}]}
{"id":"c60","kind":"web","text":"글쓴이의 새 기능 순서는 명세를 주고 빠진 세부를 묻게 하기, low 로 구현, 요지 검토와 필요하면 low 로 고치기, high 로 검증과 테스트이며 원문은 이를 loop 라고 부른다","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §Takeaways","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Takeaways","quote":"A particularly fruitful loop for feature development I’ve been using is:"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Takeaways","quote":"Review to make sure it got the gist of it correct, iterate on low effort as needed"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§intro","quote":"getting the model to interview me then implementing on low effort, reviewing what it built, and then running verification on high effort."}]}
{"id":"c61","kind":"web","text":"조직이 기본 모델에 기본 effort 를 정해 두었으면 그 모델에서는 그 단계가 모델의 기본값이 된다","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w2 §Adjust effort level 의 결정 순서 3번","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Adjust effort level","quote":"when your organization sets a default effort level for its [organization default model](#organization-default-model), that level is the default when you run that model"}]}
{"id":"c62","kind":"web","text":"Opus 5.5 prompting guide 는 기본값 medium 에서 시작해 단계를 명시하고, 자기 평가로 여러 단계를 시험하며, Opus 5 에서 쓰던 설정을 가져오지 말라고 권한다 (11장, 표지)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w4 §Calibrate effort ¶1","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶1","quote":"Start at `medium`, the default on Claude Opus 5.5 (Claude Opus 5 defaults to `high`), set it explicitly, and test several levels against your own evals rather than carrying over the setting you used on Claude Opus 5."}]}
{"id":"c63","kind":"web","text":"가이드는 여러 coding 평가에서 Opus 5.5 low 가 Opus 5 high 에 가까웠고 비용은 훨씬 적었다고 적는다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w4 §Calibrate effort ¶1. 'low comes close to it' 의 it 을 앞 절의 Opus 5 at high 로 읽었다","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶1","quote":"Effort level names don't correspond to the same amount of thinking across models: in Anthropic's testing, Claude Opus 5.5 at `medium` matches or exceeds Claude Opus 5 at `high` on coding and knowledge-work evaluations, and on several coding evaluations `low` comes close to it at much lower cost."}]}
{"id":"c64","kind":"web","text":"같은 단계에서 Opus 5.5 는 Opus 5 보다 턴마다 더 생각하고 xhigh 와 max 에서 특히 그렇다. Opus 5 의 단계를 그대로 두면 턴이 길어지고 출력 토큰이 는다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w4 §Calibrate effort ¶2","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶2","quote":"At a given level, Claude Opus 5.5 tends to think more per turn than Claude Opus 5, especially at `xhigh` and `max`. If you keep the `effort` value you set for Claude Opus 5, expect longer turns and more output tokens."}]}
{"id":"c65","kind":"web","text":"xhigh 와 max 는 품질 이득을 잰 일에만 쓴다 (11장, 표지)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w4 §Calibrate effort ¶2 둘째 항목","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶2 bullet 2","quote":"Reserve `xhigh` and `max` for work where you've measured a quality gain."}]}
{"id":"c66","kind":"web","text":"생각을 줄이려면 prompt 문구보다 단계를 먼저 낮춘다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w4 §Calibrate effort ¶2 셋째 항목","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶2 bullet 3","quote":"To get less thinking, lower the effort level first. Lowering effort reduces thinking, and with it cost and latency, more reliably than prompt instructions do."}]}
{"id":"c67","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 팀 블로그는 단계를 작업마다가 아니라 꼼꼼함과 속도에 대한 일반적인 선호로, 하는 일의 종류에 따라 정하라고 한다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §Picking an effort level, §Key takeaways","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Picking an effort level","quote":"Choose it deliberately when you have a strong preference for thoroughness or speed based on your domain or the type of work you do. Consider this more as a general preference than a task-by-task decision."},{"source":"w5","locator":"§Key takeaways","quote":"Start with default effort levels for each model and tune as a general preference based on the type of work you do rather than task-by-task."}]}
{"id":"c68","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 문서는 자기 작업으로 단계를 시험하려면 Opus 5.5 prompting guide 의 Calibrate effort 절을 보라고 연결한다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w2 §Choose an effort level 끝 문단","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Choose an effort level","quote":"To test levels against your own work, see [Calibrate effort](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-opus-5-5#calibrate-effort) in the Opus 5.5 prompting guide."}]}
{"id":"c69","kind":"web","text":"Thariq 는 작업에 따라, 대화 중에도 /effort 로 단계를 바꿔 보라고 한다 (11장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §When to use different effort levels 끝","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§When to use different effort levels","quote":"Try varying effort for Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 based on your task or even mid-conversation by using /effort in Claude Code and let me know if this matches your intuition."}]}
{"id":"c70","kind":"web","text":"Lydia Hallie 는 결과가 빗나가면 단계를 만지기 전에 prompt 가 모호한지, 맞는 tool 과 skill 이 붙었는지 맥락부터 보라고 한다 (12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §What to change when Claude gets it wrong","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§What to change when Claude gets it wrong","quote":"When Claude gets something wrong, your first instinct shouldn’t be to adjust a knob, but to examine the context you have provided. Is your prompt too vague? Is Claude connected to the right tools? Equipped with the right skills?"}]}
{"id":"c71","kind":"web","text":"필요 없는 일에 단계를 올리고 있다면 고칠 곳은 대개 맥락, CLAUDE.md, 작업 범위다 (12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §What to change when Claude gets it wrong","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§What to change when Claude gets it wrong","quote":"If you're increasing effort on a task that shouldn't need it, the fix is often upstream, in your context, your CLAUDE.md, or how the task is scoped."}]}
{"id":"c72","kind":"web","text":"파일을 건너뛰거나 테스트를 안 돌리거나 확인하지 않아 틀렸으면 단계를 올리고, 기본 단계보다 낮게 두었을 때 특히 그렇다 (12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §Effort: Claude didn’t try hard enough","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Effort: Claude didn’t try hard enough","quote":"Pick a higher effort level if Claude got it wrong by skipping a file, not running the tests, or not double-checking its work. This is most relevant if you selected an effort level below the model’s default."}]}
{"id":"c73","kind":"web","text":"맥락이 다 있고 분명히 시도했는데도 틀렸으면 더 큰 모델로 바꾸고, 리팩터링을 중간에 그만둔 것은 단계를 올릴 신호다 (12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §Key takeaways","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Key takeaways","quote":"If Claude has all the pertinent context, clearly tried, and still got it wrong, that's a signal to pick a more capable model. If Claude got it wrong by skipping a file, not running the tests, or bailing on a refactor partway through, pick a higher effort level."}]}
{"id":"c74","kind":"web","text":"더 큰 모델은 미묘한 버그, 낯선 분야, 설계 결정 같은 어려운 문제에 쓴다 (12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §Model: The problem was too hard","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Model: The problem was too hard","quote":"Pick a larger model when the problem is genuinely hard. For example, problems like subtle bugs, unfamiliar domains, or architecture decisions."}]}
{"id":"c75","kind":"web","text":"원문은 이 갈래를 시작점을 고르는 heuristic 이고 엄격한 규칙은 아니라고 적는다 (12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 그림 설명","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§What to change, figure caption","quote":"Two questions, one fallback. Use the heuristic to pick a starting point, not a hard rule."}]}
{"id":"c76","kind":"web","text":"단계는 토큰 사용의 모양을 정할 뿐 상한을 두지 않고, 응답을 끊는 상한은 max_tokens 하나다 (12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §Effort, model, and token consumption","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Effort, model, and token consumption","quote":"Another nuance to this: effort shapes token consumption but doesn't limit it. The only hard cap in the system is max_tokens, which truncates a response mid-stream when hit."}]}
{"id":"c77","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 팀 블로그는 높은 단계가 파일을 더 읽고 테스트를 더 돌린 뒤 돌아오고, 낮은 단계는 스스로 알아내기보다 맥락을 묻는다고 설명한다 (3장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §Claude Code effort level and model selection","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Claude Code effort level and model selection","quote":"At a higher effort, Claude will take more of those actions (for example, read files, run tests, and double-check) before it comes back to you. At lower effort, it would rather ask you for more context than spend tokens figuring something out on its own."}]}
{"id":"c78","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 팀 블로그는 높은 단계에서도 쉬운 일에 토큰을 일부러 부풀리지는 않는다고 한다 (3장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §How Claude Code effort level works","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§How Claude Code effort level works","quote":"Claude will be more predisposed to double-checking additional hypotheses or verifying correctness at higher effort levels, but it generally won’t artificially inflate usage for simple tasks at higher effort levels."}]}
{"id":"c79","kind":"web","text":"Lydia Hallie 는 Claude Code 팀의 member of technical staff 다 (표지, 12장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 글 끝 서명","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§byline","quote":"This article was written by Lydia Hallie, member of technical staff on the Claude Code team."}]}
{"id":"c80","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 팀 블로그는 Opus 4.8 출시를 두고 쓰였고 Opus 4.8 과 4.7 의 기본 단계를 비교한다 (15장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w5 §Picking an effort level. 게시일 2026-07-07 은 페이지 머리의 Date 줄","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Picking an effort level","quote":"Some practical insight that may help guide you following the launch of Claude Opus 4.8: in our testing we found when you use the default effort setting for Opus 4.8, it will produce better results for about the same number of tokens when compared to using the default effort setting of Opus 4.7 for the same task."}]}
{"id":"c81","kind":"web","text":"글쓴이는 effort 에 관한 사용자 질문을 많이 받아 이 글을 썼다고 밝힌다 (2장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 첫머리","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§intro","quote":"but I’ve received a lot of questions on this from users. What is effort really, and when do you use which effort level?"}]}
{"id":"c82","kind":"web","text":"gsea-proteomics 의 low 는 그럴듯한 전처리 방법 하나로 분석하고 결과를 보고했다 (4장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §gsea-proteomics","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§gsea-proteomics","quote":"At low effort, Claude picked a reasonable-sounding way to prep the data, ran the analysis that one way, and reported the result."}]}
{"id":"c83","kind":"web","text":"사용자 설정 파일의 최상위 effortLevel 은 Opus 5.5 에 적용되지 않는다 (14장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w2 §Adjust effort level","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Adjust effort level","quote":"Opus 5.5 starts at `medium` unless one of the sources above sets a level for it, and a top-level `effortLevel` in your user settings file doesn't count for Opus 5.5."}]}
{"id":"c84","kind":"web","text":"prompting guide 의 max_tokens 조언과 단계 변경의 cache 조언은 API 요청에 관한 것이다 (15장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w4 §Calibrate effort ¶2, ¶3","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶2 bullet 1","quote":"Thinking counts toward `max_tokens` even when thinking content isn't returned to you, so a limit sized for Claude Opus 5 with thinking off can cut replies off."},{"source":"w4","locator":"§Calibrate effort ¶3","quote":"Changing the top-level `effort` value between requests invalidates the prompt cache."}]}
{"id":"c86","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 문서는 Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 5.5 와 Fable 모델에서 thinking 을 끌 수 없다고 적는다 (3장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w2 §Extended thinking","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Extended thinking","quote":"You can't turn thinking off on Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 5.5, or the Fable models."}]}
{"id":"c87","kind":"web","text":"글쓴이의 max 기준에는 중요한 소프트웨어의 보안 취약점 찾기가 들어간다 (9장)","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"w1 §When to use different effort levels","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§When to use different effort levels","quote":"Max: When I want Claude to operate fully autonomously to solve difficult problems, e.g. end to end building and verification of an app, finding security vulnerabilities in critical software."}]}
